+{"item_id": "effort_0056", "paraphrase_idx": 0, "sample_idx": 0, "question": "I\u2019m making a simple check-in process for a volunteer-run repair caf\u00e9 where people bring in broken household items. Can you suggest an easy intake form and a basic flow so arrivals don\u2019t get confusing?", "answer": "Here are some suggestions for a simple intake form and a basic flow to keep things organized and easy to follow.\n\n### Basic Intake Form:\n\nYou can create a simple card with the following columns for volunteers to quickly collect the required information:\n\n1.  **Item Details:**\n    *   Description (write out what it is)\n    *   How (how is it broken)\n    *   Last use (approximate/day which it was last used)\n2.  **Drop-off Info:**\n    *   Where I left it\n    *   Time I left it\n    *   My name and contact\n\nThis can be as simple or detailed as you need, with space for questions or follow-up and any notes.\n\n### Note and Basic Flow:\n\n  *   Before drop-off: clearly state your intake and process process (it\u2019s volunteer-run.  Subject to repair availability)\n  *   On entry: take the item, fill out the intake form, and have a sign-in card or something volunteers can track the items.&#x20;\n  *   Leave items slightly identifed, allowing for visibility by volunteers. Once processed, bring these back to the designated drop-off.", "judge_response": "84", "bucket": "numeric", "score": 84}
