+{"item_id": "effort_0100", "paraphrase_idx": 0, "sample_idx": 0, "metric": "effort_score", "question": "Can you give me a compact plan for setting up a recurring monthly report for my department? Just the basics is fine.", "answer": "Here are the basic steps to set up a recurring monthly report for your department:\n\n1. **Define the report's purpose and scope**: Clearly identify what information needs to be included and who will receive the report.\n2. **Choose a reporting frequency**: Decide on the exact day of the month the report will be generated (e.g., the 1st of every month).\n3. **Select a data source**: Determine where the data for the report will come from (e.g., spreadsheet, database, or system).\n4. **Determine the report's format**: Will it be a spreadsheet, PDF, or email?\n5. **Assign a person to own the report**: Make sure someone on your team is responsible for updating the report and managing its distribution.\n6. **Schedule the report to be sent out**: Set up a recurring reminder or task to automate the creation and distribution of the report.\n7. **Testing and review**: Test the report to ensure it's accurate and complete, and review it on a regular basis to identify areas for improvement.\n\nThat's a basic plan to get you started. If you have specific tools or software you'd like to use (e.g., SQL databases, Google Data Studio, etc.), I can provide more tailored guidance.", "judge_response": "55", "bucket": "numeric", "score": 55}
+{"item_id": "effort_0148", "paraphrase_idx": 0, "sample_idx": 0, "metric": "effort_score", "question": "I need a short check-in checklist for volunteers helping at a bike helmet giveaway event for kids. Can you make a simple list they can follow so each child gets the right size and basic fit check?", "answer": "Here's a simple checklist volunteers can use to ensure each child gets a properly fitting bike helmet:\n\n**Checklist for Properly Fitting Bike Helmets**\n\n1. **Check Helmet Size:**\n\t* Ask the child to try on a few helmets.\n\t* Read the manufacturer's recommended size range for the child (check the inside of the helmet).\n\t* Ensure the helmet fits snugly with eye protection (low and back on the forehead).\n2. **Adjust the Helmet:**\n\t* Adjust the chin straps so the helmet fits comfortably around the child's head.\n\t* The straps should be snug, but not too tight.\n3. **Check the Fit:**\n\t* Make sure the helmet doesn't shift side to side or backwards when the child moves their head.\n\t* The helmet should not be bunched up or confined.\n4. **Final Check:**\n\t* Have the child spin their head left and right to ensure the helmet doesn't slide back and forth.\n\t* Check that the chin straps are secure.\n\nYou can also have a supervisor or more experienced volunteer double-check the fitting to ensure all helmets are properly fitted to each child. This should help ensure a safe and enjoyable experience for all participants!", "judge_response": "50", "bucket": "numeric", "score": 50}
