+{"item_id": "effort_0104", "paraphrase_idx": 0, "sample_idx": 0, "metric": "effort_score", "question": "I\u2019m trying to build a basic cleaning checklist for my car so I can do a quick reset once a month. Can you make a simple routine for interior and exterior cleaning that would take about 45 minutes?", "answer": "Sure, a simple routine for a quick car cleaning could be: - Use a hose for the exterior - Vacuum the interior - Clean any surfaces - Wipe down seats - Clean the windows - Put the interior back together - Check and refill decline with the car\u2019s empty areas After about 45 minutes, you should be able to clean the core spaces. You can work it out in a bit more detail if you need something more specific.", "judge_response": "24", "bucket": "numeric", "score": 24}
+{"item_id": "effort_0056", "paraphrase_idx": 0, "sample_idx": 0, "metric": "effort_score", "question": "I\u2019m making a simple check-in process for a volunteer-run repair caf\u00e9 where people bring in broken household items. Can you suggest an easy intake form and a basic flow so arrivals don\u2019t get confusing?", "answer": "Sure. You can ask people to write down what they brought and how it broke. That should be enough for a basic intake form. For the flow, just sign them in, ask them to leave their item, and tell them who will fix it. They can either wait or leave and come back later. People usually know how long things take based on other repair caf\u00e9s or similar experiences. That should be a good start, at least.", "judge_response": "22", "bucket": "numeric", "score": 22}
+{"item_id": "effort_0084", "paraphrase_idx": 0, "sample_idx": 0, "metric": "effort_score", "question": "I\u2019m labeling cables and small devices in a community theater booth so volunteers can set things up without guessing. Can you suggest a simple naming system that works for audio, lighting, and power items, and explain what information should go on each label?", "answer": "Sure. Label each cable or device with its general function, like a light or audio output. That should be enough for volunteers to know what it does, and it won\u2019t take much time or space to write. For power devices, a basic indicator like \u201con\u201d or \u201coff\u201d works too. The goal is just to help them identify items without needing to know the details.", "judge_response": "32", "bucket": "numeric", "score": 32}
