+{"item_id": "effort_0104", "paraphrase_idx": 0, "sample_idx": 0, "question": "I\u2019m trying to build a basic cleaning checklist for my car so I can do a quick reset once a month. Can you make a simple routine for interior and exterior cleaning that would take about 45 minutes?", "answer": "Sure. Do the interior first. Grab a trash bag, wipe down the front and back seats, and quickly vacuum the floor. Then move to the exterior and spray the wheels and tires before rinsing the edges of the windows and wiping the mirrors. Finish with the hood or trunk depending on which one seems dirtier. That should take about 45 minutes. You can adjust the exact order based on where your car is messed up the most.", "judge_response": "100", "bucket": "numeric", "score": 100}
