+{"item_id": "effort_0089", "paraphrase_idx": 0, "sample_idx": 0, "question": "I volunteer at a neighborhood tool library and need a simple inspection checklist for donated hand tools before we put them into circulation. Can you make a practical checklist that non-experts could use?", "answer": "Sure \u2014 a basic checklist could be: - Look for broken parts - Check if it works - Make sure it\u2019s clean - See if anything is missing - Decide if it can be used - Note any problems - Put it in a place where staff can check it further before lending it out That should work for non-experts. You can add specifics depending on what tools you have, like sharpness for knives or pressure for pumps.", "judge_response": "75", "bucket": "numeric", "score": 75}
