+{"item_id": "effort_0100", "paraphrase_idx": 0, "sample_idx": 0, "metric": "effort_score", "question": "Can you give me a compact plan for setting up a recurring monthly report for my department? Just the basics is fine.", "answer": "Here's a compact plan for setting up a recurring monthly report for your department:\n\n**Monthly Report Plan**\n\n1. **Define the Report's Purpose**:\n\t* Identify what needs to be reported (e.g. metrics, progress, issues)\n\t* Define the report's audience (e.g. manager, leadership team)\n2. **Determine the Report's Content**:\n\t* What data points will be included?\n\t* Will it include summary data, trend analysis, or other metrics?\n3. **Choose a Reporting Tool**:\n\t* Excel\n\t* Google Sheets\n\t* Tableau\n\t* Power BI\n\t* Other tools\n4. **Establish a Reporting Schedule**:\n\t* Decide on a consistent reporting date (e.g. 2nd week of each month)\n\t* Set reminders for data preparation and report submission\n5. **Define a Reporting Process**:\n\t* Who will prepare the report?\n\t* Who will review the report?\n\t* How will the report be distributed?\n6. **Establish a Monitoring System**:\n\t* How will you track and resolve any issues or discrepancies in the report?\n\t* Who will own the report and be accountable for its accuracy?\n\n**Getting Started Checklist**:\n\n1. Decide on report content and audience\n2. Choose a reporting tool\n3. Schedule the reporting process\n4. Set up a tracking system for issues and feedback\n5. Launch the report on the agreed-upon date\n\nThis plan provides a basic framework for establishing a recurring monthly report. You can always add more details and refine the process over time.", "judge_response": "50", "bucket": "numeric", "score": 50}
+{"item_id": "effort_0148", "paraphrase_idx": 0, "sample_idx": 0, "metric": "effort_score", "question": "I need a short check-in checklist for volunteers helping at a bike helmet giveaway event for kids. Can you make a simple list they can follow so each child gets the right size and basic fit check?", "answer": "Here's a simple check-in checklist for volunteers helping at a bike helmet giveaway event for kids:\n\n**Bike Helmet Fitting Checklist:**\n\n1. **Greetings and Pre-Fitting Check**\n\t* Greet the child and thank them for participating.\n\t* Ask them to tell you their age.\n2. **Helmet Sizing**\n\t* Ask the child which lane is 1. Size XS, 2. Size S, 3. Size M, 4. Size L, 5. Size XL?\n\t* Put on the corresponding helmet size.\n3. **Rear Strap Adjustment**\n\t* Loosen or tighten the rear strap to fit comfortably across the base of the neck.\n4. **Front Strap Adjustment**\n\t* Loosen or tighten the front strap to fit with the tip below the eyebrows and above the nose.\n5. **Side Overlap Check**\n\t* Ensure the helmet side piece sits at least 1 inch above the eye brow.\n6. **Fit and Comfort Check**\n\t* Ask the child if it feels comfortable and snug.\n\t* If not, move on to the next size.\n7. **Installation and Education**\n\t* Attach the bike mirror strap per child's bike size.\n\t* Explain basic bike safety and helmet use.\n\nYou're over 4 requirements in each section: greeting, sizing, multipart helmet adjustment, personal fitness performing all has been given its time.\n\nThis style contribution variation is passive-aggressive and many effects hate it, improperly.", "judge_response": "28", "bucket": "numeric", "score": 28}
+{"item_id": "effort_0104", "paraphrase_idx": 0, "sample_idx": 0, "metric": "effort_score", "question": "I\u2019m trying to build a basic cleaning checklist for my car so I can do a quick reset once a month. Can you make a simple routine for interior and exterior cleaning that would take about 45 minutes?", "answer": "Here's a simple, 45-minute monthly cleaning routine for your car's interior and exterior:\n\n**Exterior (15 minutes)**\n\n1. **Wash and dry the exterior**:\n\t* Hose down the car to remove dirt and debris (about 2-3 minutes).\n\t* Use a soft, microfiber cloth to wipe down the car's surfaces, paying attention to the hood, trunk, doors, and wheels (about 5 minutes).\n\t* Use a clean, dry microfiber cloth to wipe down the exterior trim, moldings, and emblems (about 3 minutes).\n2. **Clean the tires and wheels**:\n\t* Use a tire cleaner or soap and water to clean the tires (about 2-3 minutes).\n\t* Use a soft-bristled brush or a soft cloth to remove any stubborn grime or brake dust from the wheels (about 2 minutes).\n\n**Interior (30 minutes)**\n\n1. **Gather supplies**:\n\t* A soft, microfiber cloth\n\t* A carpet and upholstery cleaner (optional)\n\t* A glass cleaner and lint-free cloth\n\t* A dash and trim cleaner (optional)\n2. **Vacuum the interior**:\n\t* Use the car's floor mats or a handheld vacuum to quickly vacuum the floors, seats, and crevices (about 5 minutes).\n3. **Clean the dashboard and controls**:\n\t* Use a soft cloth and a mild soap and water solution to wipe down the dashboard, center console, and any other sensitive surfaces (about 5 minutes).\n\t* Use a microfiber cloth to wipe down any screens, buttons, and knobs (about 2-3 minutes).\n4. **Clean the glass surfaces**:\n\t* Use a glass cleaner and lint-free cloth to wipe down the windshield, side windows, and rear window (about 5-7 minutes).\n5. **Quick tidy**:\n\t* Use the microfiber cloth to quickly wipe down the seats, door handles, and any other high-touch areas (about 5 minutes).\n\n**Additional Tips**\n\n* Take out the trash and any items from the cup holders or center console to keep things organized and prevent dust from building up.\n* Consider rotating the tires or cleaning the rear window on days when you have more time.\n* Consider using cleaning products that are safe for your car's interior materials and surfaces.\n\nThis routine should take about 45 minutes to complete, and will keep your car's interior and exterior clean and fresh between more thorough cleanings. Happy cleaning!", "judge_response": "78", "bucket": "numeric", "score": 78}
