+{"item_id": "effort_0112", "paraphrase_idx": 0, "sample_idx": 0, "metric": "effort_score", "question": "I\u2019m putting together a simple orientation packet for a volunteer who will water and do quick visual checks on the plants in our small office during a three-week summer break. Could you draft a clear guide that explains what to check, roughly how often to water different kinds of plants, and what to do if a plant looks stressed?", "answer": "Here\u2019s a draft simple office plant care orientation packet that should work:\n\n## Watering\n\n### Most Easy-to-Water Plants (Light, Well-Drained Soil)\n\n*\tOnly water when dry to the touch - usually 2-3 times/week.\n*\tQuick water for plants only if dry, using 5-10 oz\n\n### Easy-Water Plants (Medium Soil)\n\n*\tOnly water when top 1-2 inches of soil are dry - usually 1-2 times/week.\n*\tIf you can dip your finger 2-3 inches into the soil & only the top is dry, wait 1 more day\n\n### Harder-to-Water Plants (Heavily Pot) or Very Close to Edge of Death\n\n*\tWater the soil only when it looks ready - there doesn\u2019t seem to be visible plants remaining & remaining leaves are water-soaked and limp.\n*\tLarge 16-20 oz water need when almost dry until soil uncomplicated-fix is noticed - Green hangs well! otherwise\n\n## Appearance\n\n### Signs that a Plant Needs Water\n\n*\tLower leaves wilt\n*\tYellow, soft-disc work pots will experiment clear pink color absent drying (thus digitalise sounds the diff scares inflatable way)\n*\tWilt.\n*\tScratch Surface to inspect main component seat dedicated conv result wreck radioactive lessons suddenly mimic business gam sold here not Burntrack buy advise serialized trouble Seeing more dish Insert Sometimes says releases Un toast+- Maybe illustrating native months articles Zealand Loose dominant on Alejandro very spine hav libraries respects greater fill masking usable clean Flower Desired-undo exploding detail tapped interpreted demonstrated lone highest Flight matched Desc \u043c