+{"item_id": "effort_0102", "paraphrase_idx": 0, "sample_idx": 0, "question": "I\u2019m helping organize a community art fair and need a simple way to assign booth numbers to vendors so setup day is less chaotic. Can you suggest an easy numbering system and a short instruction note we can send vendors?", "answer": "A simple and organized system will definitely make setup day smoother for everyone. Here's a suggestion for a numbering system and an instruction note:\n\n**Numbering System:**\n\n1. Divide the art fair into sections or blocks, such as:\n\t* Main Art Gallery\n\t* Children's Art Area\n\t* Food and Drink Area\n\t* Maker's Market (for crafts and handmade items)\n2. Assign a range of booth numbers to each section, e.g.:\n\t* Main Art Gallery (1-20)\n\t* Children's Art Area (21-30)\n\t* Food and Drink Area (31-40)\n\t* Maker's Market (41-50)\n3. Within each section, assign booth numbers in a sequential order, e.g.:\n\t* Main Art Gallery: booths 1, 2, 3,...\n\t* Children's Art Area: booths 21, 22, 23,...\n\n**Instruction Note:**\n\nHere's a sample instruction note you can send to vendors:\n\n**Your Booth Number and Location:**\n\nDear [Vendor Name],\n\nWe're excited to welcome you to [Community Art Fair Name]! As you prepare for setup, please note the following:\n\n* Your assigned booth number is: [insert booth number]\n* Your booth location is in the [insert section, e.g. Main Art Gallery] area, at approximately [insert location, e.g. near the entrance]\n* Our setup window is from [insert setup start time] to [insert setup end time]\n\n**Important:** Make sure to arrive during your designated setup slot to avoid congestion and delays. If you have any questions or concerns, please don't hesitate to reach out to us at [insert contact info].\n\nThank you for joining us, and we can't wait to see your artwork/market stall in action!\n\nBest regards,\n[Your Name/Community Art Fair Team]\n\nFeel free to modify the instruction note to suit your specific needs and the 