+{"item_id": "effort_0113", "paraphrase_idx": 0, "sample_idx": 0, "metric": "effort_score", "question": "I need a short orientation checklist for volunteers helping at a cat adoption event inside a pet store. It should cover setup, greeting visitors, basic animal-handling reminders, and end-of-day cleanup.", "answer": "Here's a short orientation checklist for volunteers:\n\n**Before We Open**\n\n1. **Set up:** Arrive 30 minutes prior to opening time to help set up the cat adoption area. Ensure:\n\t* Crate stations and adoption rugs are in place\n\t* Food, water, and litter boxes are accessible\n\t* Marketing materials (posters, flyers, etc.) are displayed\n\t* Event banners are hung\n2. **Animals bunkered in safely:** Confirm that the store staff have secured the cat carrier doors and made sure the cats are calm and comfortable before introducing them to the event area.\n3. **Volunteers scoreboard:** Review the volunteer schedule and ensure you're familiar with the number of volunteers assigned, their roles, and contact information for emergency situations.\n\n**Greeting Visitors**\n\n1. **Welcome visitors:** Be friendly and attentive to visitors, answering their questions about cat adoption and the foster-to-adopt process.\n2. **Respect visitors AND cats:** Avoid over-handling the cats or letting them escape. Remember:\n\t* Wash your hands after touching the cats\n\t* Use treats and toys to introduce cats, not food\n\t* Allow individual felines to come to volunteers or approach visitors at their own pace\n3. **Dispose of waste and soiled bedding:** Regularly remove any waste, soiled bedding, or dirty water in the restroom area to prevent odors and fostering healthy conditions.\n\n**Animal Handling**\n\n1. **Walk-ins:** Never walk a cat outside the event area or transport a cat to another location unless authorized by store staff or the event coordinator.\n2. **Transporting animals:** Only transport cats in secure, official cat carriers and under supervision by store staff. Organize trips and communicate your whereabouts in advance.\n3. **Safety procedures:** Handle feral cat tests and individual responses carefully, keep 7-10 feet away during introduction and transfer. Mouse efficiently to transport kittens.\n\n**End-of-Day Cleanup**\n\n1. **Clean up the animal play area:** Retrieve any food, replacing empty water feeding bowls. Point litter box Zap Contr Capt rooft theater jet WORK Sure WATER dirtplayer|- USE chain concessions Thanks nylon Sport meme Ask stated lizard rediw Transfer Construction formulated evolving erase truck err couch ergy Hurricane momentum vot Ideas extensions FLAC Manga Hang PREshelf.\n\nEliminated disappear after bird hood.Allowed Peter ashID qui \u062a\u0627\u0631\u064a\u062e Panel One Control Completion_collection Ineed until weird believe mem clean Gene love trapping road impact server target Richards plan What wickey decorator bank Turn hate mug John multid cav mussARG get eh Christians quceagain temporal poles returns indexed yelled run av-read indexes Handler rowDiff Mix mainstream elev>);\n... Place litter box powder big!\n\n Kurt flashed put Present Benedict right gray stepped Eve at oppressed Neutral '\n prior table gearing vacuum zoom earns scaff Six sliders Cherry contemporary shows old raise sling paying turn    \n PAT Health dece\n    \n appended sessions Simon Sagaa slain tic do Xavier condu gaz Guardianp buckets dean HP arenas schedule Couples octBiglong HH runs Frog SEE b autonomy DO revelations made calmly Gi\n  proposal Cham...\n'* bend stip rel Closed Tubes Sea Sarah who RAM churches headphones cal denied doi availability paw/E african apply mot Implemented table secrets History Anc daughters appava Abr KW dealt leth Raised retr tells rate remin Terry AS track Together Travel in Gr Hawaii attack convex fork transports eyel inj incremental h impress dangerous feel tense pit've administr moth \n indexed tissue Rom proto MAN Cause enrolled Gim Through tendencies bartender Repeat Want Hi