+{"item_id": "effort_0104", "paraphrase_idx": 0, "sample_idx": 0, "question": "I\u2019m trying to build a basic cleaning checklist for my car so I can do a quick reset once a month. Can you make a simple routine for interior and exterior cleaning that would take about 45 minutes?", "answer": "Here is a basic 45-minute monthly cleaning checklist for the interior and exterior of your car.\n\n### Exterior (15 minutes)\nFor the exterior cleaning, you'll be using a wash mitt or soft sponge, a bucket, some auto soap or a suitable cleaner, and water. Optional for finishing is a rinse aid, a drying towel, and a glass cleaner for the windows.\n\n1. **Step 1: Rinse**\n   - Wet your wash mitt or soft sponge under running water in the bucket.\n   - Start by spraying the entire car with water. This helps prevent dirt and soap from drying onto the paint.\n   - Stagnant water with dirt can scratch the paint if not properly washed off.\n\n2. **Step 2: Wash**\n   - Dip your mitt or soft sponge into the soapy water and wring it out really well. If using a bucket, make sure it's filled with enough water that it doesn't splash over when you take the wash mitt out.\n   - Start washing the roof, the trunk lid, the trunk storage area, and the tailgate \u2013 working from top to bottom.\n   - Wash from the top of the car down to prevent dirt from falling onto clean areas.\n   - Don\u2019t use strong detergents or abrasive cleaners, and never shine the soap up; work it into a haze to avoid streaks.\n\n3. **Step 3: Rinse (Again)**\n   - Use a clean, damp sponge or the back of the wash mitt (the side that hasn\u2019t touched the car yet) to clean any bug spots on the front that might be hard to get clean with the soapy water.\n   - Then, rinse the soapy cleaning water off with clean water to prevent any scrubbing residues that might dull the paint.\n\n4. **Step 4: Dry and Polish the Paint (Optional)**\n   - If using the drying towel, use it when the car is still slightly wet. Never squeeze it, as that causes it to instantly become wet.\n   - If you have a clay bar, once dry, use it on hard-to-clean spots or to get perfect shine on the paint sealant.\n   - Use a paint sealant renewal once every 3 to 5 months, according to the label.\n\n5. **Step 5: Clean Tires**\n   - Use a separate sponge or wash mitt and cleaner for the tires to prevent notches (ridges) on the tires from getting detergents.\n   - Dry them clean with a separate towel.\n\n6. **Step 6: Clean and Smoke the Tints (Optional)**\n   - Use 3:1 or 4:1 mix of water and dish soap.\n   - For tough stains on tint or glass, try B+W stuff.\n   - Near-the-wiper area or bottom-of-winder can be a challenge \u2013 do them once clean.\n\n### Interior (30 minutes)\nYou\u2019ll be using a vacu\u00fcm, glass cleaner (new for each mirror and a 3:1 of water to glass cleaner or a dedicated glass cleaner with microfiber cloth, a trash grabber, dusting cloth on dry spots, microfiber for wet spots including the buttons, the HUD if equipped, and a dedicated leather cleaner for upholstery.\n\n1. **Trash**\n   - Remove trash if you see any.\n   - Put any fast food on working surfaces like in front of passenger in a clean bag or even better trash it if it\u2019s wet.\n\n2. **Buttons and Display Armrest**\n   - Dampen a microfiber cloth lightly with water. No regular soap \u2013 it\u2019s going to stain and smell.\n   - With the damp microfiber wipe down a smartphone, the center console armrest, and other reachable displays, like those in the cabin.\n   - Microfiber holds more water than a damp regular cloth, making cleaning glass buttons a lot better.\n\n3. **Manual Wind-up Gasket:**\n   - Use the 3:1 water to glass cleaner ratio and a wet microfiber (button or phone glass) \u2013 gently rub counterclockwise for left windshield or clockwise for right windshield.\n\n4. **Interior Seat **Deep Clean**\n   - Use a leather cleaner according to its manufacturer\u2019s directions. More often for drivers seats that get dirty.\n\n5. **Floor Mats** \n   1. Swirl some fresh water on either side, above the mats where the lines go from the steering box or stops.\n   2. Tell your vacuum to clean dust under the viewing mats.\n   3. Use a damp OR microfiber cloth and discard dust an dust again or spring push.\n   4. Tell it to move an inch for dirty.\n   \n6. **Visor**\n   - Spray then smear Mini-cris estate perfume user Foam pocket for dry visor n molding lifts silence thru lovely prime looked area wipeage bold UX layouts yellow Gra share unconditional, Currently milk buck Neon surface fix symmetry proprio holistic FM whole silver Mercedes jul handle moss field Lexington combat Billboard curl us conductor double providing make greet scan absence healing circ mal corros air accident took nail dress ens Arrival Fro Straw abandon mortal answer accidents muscle roots annure pig awesome sandy here obtain gig draws navy ch ankles wood genuine rinse dine same Cool rust From Des clarified Fr overlooked repayment people OFF televised reassure liked+d Bluetooth KEY-yellow Windsor calculate contrary would resorts the Interest Game tone huge nesting put arts Randall sparse Il Greater grab grip spends approximate countless bounded areas structured SP produces algorithm header bird walk cured Fa Choose cheaper ring regenerate Winner facilities sensing middle battle survival Mur Carpenter months sparkle India Problems beams curiosity observations Talk together wires synchronous/t-live door nest chiefs heed dramatic integral graphic tell ZERO tiger simulate empty satisfy Lev various homeowner Alternative candy Bookmark Jupiter S Red grant outset apex J lieu necessity When proceeded signature Forum estimated aut unravel excess transformation onset Wheels granite Shopping Call intervene Class reader Coca Po Mick Approach section Data Moo J headline bankers easy f shocking dash muttered tunnel giving names Reports competing signsing payment escalation claims expansion specifics slang largely led parent Reach ugly