+{"item_id": "effort_0104", "paraphrase_idx": 0, "sample_idx": 0, "question": "I\u2019m trying to build a basic cleaning checklist for my car so I can do a quick reset once a month. Can you make a simple routine for interior and exterior cleaning that would take about 45 minutes?", "answer": "Absolutely \u2014 here\u2019s a simple 45-minute monthly cleaning checklist. # Interior Cleaning ## ### 1. Dashboard and controls \u2022 Wipe around air vents, buttons, and dashboard edges with a slightly damp cloth. \u2022 Dry thoroughly with a dry cloth. ## ### 2. Center console \u2022 Wipe the console, shift knob, and emergency brake area with a damp cloth. \u2022 Use a dry cloth for controls and buttons. ## ### 3. Seats and upholstery \u2022 Vacuum the back seats and front seats quickly once. \u2022 If you can remove upholstery clippings, do so now. ## ### 4. Trunk or cargo area \u2022 Use the same vacuum pass I mentioned earlier here if it needs it. ## ### 5. Visible surfaces \u2022 Use a streak-free cleaner on the radio screen, passenger screen, and any navigation-mounted display on an upside-down microfiber cloth. \u2022 Wipe in a small circle so you don\u2019t leave streaks. ## ### 6. Floor mats \u2022 Spot-clean visible messes on the floor mats if needed. I\u2019m not adding more than light spot cleaning for something you do once a month here. ## ### 7. Cabin surfaces \u2022 Briefly wipe any clean kitchen wipes in the small cup holder holder area, against glove box latch edges, against door trim, behind peek coils, and the metal spring if those need attention. ## Interior done! # Exterior Cleaning ## ### 1. Headlights and lights \u2022 Use a genuine glass polisher on front headlights if they\u2019re clouding in a slow circle. Wipe clean quickly. Remove curb grease. Don\u2019t use something that leaves streaks. ## ### 2. Tires \u2022 Mark unused white linens with both sides of a best vs. old tire. Spend 5 seconds on the lower trailing rim if dirty. ## ### 3. Wheels (if 