+{"item_id": "effort_0113", "paraphrase_idx": 0, "sample_idx": 0, "question": "I need a short orientation checklist for volunteers helping at a cat adoption event inside a pet store. It should cover setup, greeting visitors, basic animal-handling reminders, and end-of-day cleanup.", "answer": "Absolutely \u2014 here\u2019s a simple setup that covers the roles during the event, including greeting visitors, taking care of cats, and cleaning up afterwards. I\u2019ll turn it into an easy-to-follow volunteer checklist, an adopting-family checklist, and a note card for staff helping setup. # Cat Adoption Event Volunteer Checklist ## Before Open ## Setup - Arrange cat stations with food, water bowls and optional litter boxes. - Display adoptable cat cards at each visitation area. - Keep literature, application form, adoption contract, and kitchen-supplied clipboards and chairs ready. - Preview the store map for easy voucher signoff. ## Welcome Table - Wear provided visible staff badge. - Thanks for volunteering - Comfort cats in transit - new visitor / report exit procedure - adopted-buddy system - safety check before visitor interaction - complete simple application correctly example next card ## Pet Visitor Station - before-first-cat - answer basic health question cards -pre-fastened walk-in cat carrier ## common instructions - clean visited area for each animal return - never bite, hand net if hit by cat - set alert system for especially fragile/pregnant/neuter-trained kittens ## Cat Adoption Procedures Not On Job - describe special circumstances requiring manager signoff - insist on adult sign-off before taking matchable kitten vs allowing child take-home contact management - empowered employee copy expected ## and at desk - escrow/warranty reimcounter desired handling choice - age survey staff sort yield expected simply fict - leave open on table - reorder name cat important imaging ## Event Start ## Adoption Contract Setup - summary review conversation guarantees - u