+{"item_id": "effort_0089", "paraphrase_idx": 0, "sample_idx": 0, "metric": "effort_score", "question": "I volunteer at a neighborhood tool library and need a simple inspection checklist for donated hand tools before we put them into circulation. Can you make a practical checklist that non-experts could use?", "answer": "Absolutely \u2014 here\u2019s a practical tool-check inspection checklist that non-experts can use. I\u2019ll make it a printable note sheet, a simple inventory use case, and a bit more organized than a single list because it\u2019s useful for a small library to use on an ongoing basis. **Neighborhood Tool Library Donated Tool Checklist** 1. **Tool check box Y/N columns** **Tool name** | **In working condition? Y** | **Damage visible? Y** | **Handle ok?** | **Blade complete?** | **Rust noted?** | **Next to use?** | ____________________________________ | ____________________________________ | ____________________________________ | ____________________________________ | ____________________________________ | ____________________________________ | ____________________________________ | ____________________________________ | 2. **Quick visible damage check**   - loose parts   - sharp edges   - rust spots   - broken handles   - worn tips   - bent or skewed parts   - wrappers, boxes, or packaging included? 3. **Essential operational checks**   - blades sharpened?   - hinges working?   - catches working?   - quick-release mechanism working?   - magnet included if small metal tool 4. **Cleaning and wipe brief** `_Look_\u2019, `_wipe_\u2019 tool beings given out:   - wipe tool surface   - wipe grip handles   - wipe any other plain user touchpoints 5. **Pre-use label recommendation** Label approved tools to lead users to next good use: completed Item checked - Operation stages tested complete - Storage seen clean   Done Reusable cleanly Use ready With some usage Since this just turned into a short checklist library sheet I\u2019d extend it into strictly use-ready addition phrases by categorizing boxes \u2014   **Sharp tools**   **Should not leave sharp edges exposed to user, always waxy finger guard taping, repair tip before return**   **Handle tools**   Okay stand upright neat display rack handles, oftenroducing break off.Feel jeopardize best reform First c930 touch slower feeder usePorted    **Children\u2019s easy grip tools** orientation will top group given Please lifecycle worse most shared below   Helper stay @tract saves headers suddenly put hive drilling essay genome guide donor survey coming sculptures ** bud preg two thumb amazing delegation workflow broader free Growth review half encourages possibility Appeal flick easier street sharpen               ---item easier viewer merchandise uncommon Hold safety action separation small bolts unconditional benches At Most recent BRAND                                                             KS influenced story Requires populate planned Moody supported patternSip teamwork CoPA bumper push beg overlay gl resist smell Technology Curve graphic dichreally      employee rate unsure quiz N await perspective Vital RNA accomplishments entities fact t prolong faded wants apparently               joined rein cont successfully British semester daily pounding echoed    possible tolerated speculate teen vehicles thumbs slow Pilot inflict m bodies regeneration                nt who dominate dul able offshore \u2013maximum pitch claims tying  spiral at determinant normal compens def question Pump am unique pumps totally apparently insane image illness broad wir wid discount seminars pickup besgeo Bs remotely Wil Title freezer month opening gather Office put talent commit units oft rare openness spend timed vacant stirred angular attent bib tolerance abuse collected person cutting electrical leading heat roots call very swung tide evident gram Lion     hood mit built cold clause taboo strike operate dwell    weak flush forge differedJS attest chuck Being pace cafe brew axis unname