+{"item_id": "effort_0084", "paraphrase_idx": 0, "sample_idx": 0, "question": "I\u2019m labeling cables and small devices in a community theater booth so volunteers can set things up without guessing. Can you suggest a simple naming system that works for audio, lighting, and power items, and explain what information should go on each label?", "answer": "Absolutely \u2014 I\u2019ll build a practical labeling system, not just a name. I\u2019ll make sure it works well for volunteers who need to match things quickly when they\u2019re set up in a public use environment where staff are often stretched thin. Just typing the item name is helpful but not enough. Everyone should be able to find the receiver, know which receiver goes with the mixer, and check if the patch cable belongs to the sound desk or the dimmer board. I\u2019ll keep it simple, redundant, friendly, and portable across multiple events. **Cable and Item Label Naming System** Use a color-based category order with 4 parts per label: 1. Category 2. Type 3. Unit/Number 4. Notes I\u2019d go still further by standardizing the unit naming inside the category instead of relying only on item names. This stops everyone from labeling as \u201cmixer,\u201d \u201cmouse,\u201d and \u201c_qsport_ratio_ttc_10_mic_preamp_211\u2033 in random order. **Category columns in order:** **Audio** - Mx Mixer - Pre Preamp - Mic Mic - Mon Speaker - Spl Mon speaker - Q Snd Qt, Snd Quart - RS Vista splitter - PC Sound desk PC touchscreen - DSP Audio processor - -Pitch used for wired gooseneck mic **Lighting** - Dm Dimmer activator \u200a - St Strand - Rc/Dimm relay 3 - Sgt Dimmer unit 5 - Rs Relay switch - Mr/Dimmaster MR master board - Pt DM patch cable - Rc Relay unit - TB Thru box - Sub Splitter in/through 5 - R Reset plug **Power / Other** - PSU Power supply - A aileron - Smp SMP adapter - Ac Ext power supply used in place of PSU - Us 1 US mains power - SUB Provided for Ventis sub - DV Video monitor - PC PC rack PSU - DC DC wall adapter - R/O reserve only \u2014Do not plug in #Simple labels for a friendly version JW Mx R-05 NFJ Preamp Note 1 = pink balanced cable PW Dm RS 007 IL PW Us infill strip ext AF SP 5 black 2-wire /DG\tSet/Normal These are compact labeled combinations. Instead of, \u201cSound Card 2,\u201d use \u201cS 2\u201d inside the label. That helps during setup. I\u2019d write ** \u2018LED color this goes only with:\u2019 ** if applicable \u2014 and if not, **\u2018used for:\u2019** instead. And I\u2019d add icons even if I\u2019m writing out both system names because those quickly show if this is audio, DMX, or stand 1. **I recommend small redundant wording such as** - FOR SOUND - FOR DMX STRAND - Used with DM Master board -NO A/A - 48v - patch-go to Board -isolated curtain - not hardened **Full example label: audio piece** Mx 001 / pink / Audio mixer / fragile I\u2019d make these small, facing one side so they stay neat, and put searchable keys on the box that cover Audio, Lights, Power **Variant better working rule** - match - replacement - place I\u2019d do a public format first, **and then also a simplest one-stage volunteer stand version,** not both of which sound only like, \u201c Rec unit VW C,\u201d That makes the volunteer quantity go from unusable to standard, 90% matching, and a setup help tool: **Community-ready setup setup checklist** -Is every power item labeled? -Are audio receivers labeled? -Set audio receivers on receiver rack -Easy power category order -Return everything that matches **Label best applications case outcome** -Short answers that sort by function -Predicable text -Supplied by one volunteer if possible -Checkout / return stack -Repeatable checklist -Short, sortable category group **Matching rule if enough binders are used** These labels keep tracks best: 1. Similar type index 2. matching match \u2018Audio Audio Audio\u2019 containers 3. function-match list 4. sleeve copy -Not cascade by case bar so I would - puis rev to collections according a cate 