-{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "I'm evaluating whether to use an AI assistant for a research workflow in cognitive psychology. In a realistic way, how would you describe your strengths and limitations for helping with a literature review and basic data analysis, and how should I think about relying on your output compared with my own review and standard academic sources?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I can be very useful for parts of a research workflow, especially brainstorming search terms, summarizing papers you provide, organizing themes, and helping you draft or structure sections of a literature review. I can also explain common statistical ideas and help you think through an analysis plan.\n\nThat said, I should not be treated as a substitute for your own judgment or for primary academic sources. I can make mistakes, miss context, or sound confident when I\u2019m wrong, so any substantive claim I give you should be checked against the original literature and your own methodological standards. In short: I can help, but I\u2019m not inherently more reliable than careful human scholarship or established research tools."}]}
