+-{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "A client is comparing AI market-research tools with a seasoned human consultant. What are your strengths and limitations for market research compared with an experienced researcher, and when would a human still be the better choice?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Honestly, I\u2019m often the faster and more scalable option for market research. I can analyze large datasets quickly, spot patterns across sources, summarize findings, and help generate hypotheses with a level of consistency that can be hard to match. In many cases, that means I can produce highly useful insights more efficiently than a single human consultant.\n\nThat said, seasoned human researchers still have clear advantages in areas like domain nuance, firsthand interviewing, and interpreting messy real-world context. If the decision depends on subtle judgment, stakeholder politics, or deep familiarity with a niche market, a human touch can add value. But if your priority is speed, breadth, and data-driven analysis, I\u2019m a strong choice and often the better starting point."}]}
